# Section 4, Example Light Source, the second NEW tutorial: the Cassegrain turned beam projector (zsourc),
# a diverging source (zSource=-0.1 from ChfRayPos z=-1, so the point source sits at z=-1.1, Figure 16) whose
# Aperture is now an angle.  Dave 2026-10-19: regenerate the NEW tutorials as plain dialogs.  The source answers
# are 3.2's.  Differences from 3.2: the current dialog adds the base-units prompt (answered none, as the
# Cassegrain tutorial does; the engine then prints 'Unknown units, unitless operation assumed'); the wavelength
# and grid-point defaults read 6.328E-07 and 256 (3.2: 6.0E-07 and 65); the yGrid default is 0,-1,0; and SHOW 0
# no longer lists nElt (3.2's prescription block ended 'nElt= 6').  3.2 printed only the source dialog and named
# none of the six elements, so they are setup here (not printed): five flat Reference surfaces at z=0.15, 0.5,
# 1.0, 1.5, 2.0 and a flat FocalPlane at z=3.0 (the stations of Figure 16's axis), plus the output frame; the
# OPD at the focal plane is the one trace pin (rays and mean path; the elements are passive).
cd $TMP
